<body>
    <h1>Development Workflow</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This document describes the standard development workflow for th=
e IDGraph Events Helper project.</p>
<p><style type=3D"text/css">/*<![CDATA[*/
div.rbtoc1786801955026 {padding: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1786801955026 ul {margin-left: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1786801955026 li {margin-left: 0px;padding-left: 0px;}

/*]]>*/</style></p>
<div class=3D"toc-macro rbtoc1786801955026">
<ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
<li><a href=3D"#DevelopmentWorkflow-Diagram">Diagram</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#DevelopmentWorkflow-Steps">Steps</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"DevelopmentWorkflow-Diagram">Diagram</h2>
<p><br></p>
<p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:984px;m=
ax-width: 100%;" src=3D"86753787ac5ff7f0feac9baa6adde17de97eb3c0bf104c5f03d=
606350ddd9f08" height=3D"1228"></p>
<p><code class=3D"language-mermaid"> </code></p>
<h2 id=3D"DevelopmentWorkflow-Steps">Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Clone Repository</strong>: Get the latest code from the remote =
repository.</li>
<li><strong>Create Feature Branch</strong>: Use a descriptive branch name (=
e.g., <code>feature/new-publisher</code> or <code>bugfix/exception-handling=
</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Implement Feature / Fix Bug</strong>: Make code changes as need=
ed.</li>
<li><strong>Write/Update Unit Tests</strong>: Ensure new code is covered by=
 unit tests.</li>
<li><strong>Write/Update Component Tests</strong>: Add or update component-=
level tests for new or changed functionality.</li>
<li><strong>Run Tests Locally</strong>: Use <code>mvn clean install</code> =
to verify all tests pass.</li>
<li><strong>Check Code Coverage</strong>: Review test coverage reports (e.g=
., Jacoco, Cobertura).</li>
<li><strong>Coverage Sufficient?</strong>: If not, improve/add tests and re=
run tests.</li>
<li><strong>Check Code Quality</strong>: Run static analysis tools (e.g., S=
onarQube, Checkstyle, PMD).</li>
<li><strong>Quality Passes?</strong>: If not, fix code quality issues and r=
erun tests.</li>
<li><strong>Commit Changes</strong>: Write clear, concise commit messages.<=
/li>
<li><strong>Push Branch to Remote</strong>: Push your branch to the remote =
repository.</li>
<li><strong>Open Pull Request</strong>: Create a PR for review.</li>
<li><strong>Code Review</strong>: Address feedback from reviewers.</li>
<li><strong>Approved?</strong>: If approved, proceed to merge. If not, fix =
review comments and return to code review.</li>
<li><strong>Fix Review Comments</strong>: Address reviewer feedback and upd=
ate your PR.</li>
<li><strong>Merge to Master</strong>: After approval, merge your branch.</l=
i>
<li><strong>Trigger Build on master branch</strong>: Automated build and de=
ployment are triggered (This will deploy master branch code to DEV2 US East=
).</li>
<li><strong>Sanity Test in DEV2</strong>: Perform a basic validation of the=
 deployed build in the DEV2 environment.</li>
<li><strong>Review SonarQube for code coverage and code duplicate</strong>:=
 Check SonarQube dashboard for code coverage and duplication issues after b=
uild.</li>
<li><strong>Review Veracode</strong>: Review Veracode scan results for secu=
rity vulnerabilities after build.</li>
<li><strong>Promote build to TEST2</strong>: Move the validated build from =
DEV2 to the TEST2 environment for further testing (after all parallel check=
s pass).</li>
<li><strong>Sanity Test in TEST2</strong>: Perform a basic validation of th=
e deployed build in the TEST2 environment.</li>
<li><strong>QA Verification in TEST2</strong>: Request QA team to perform f=
eature and regression testing in TEST2.</li>
<li><strong>Wait for QA confirmation</strong>: Wait for QA team to confirm =
successful testing in TEST2.</li>
<li><strong>Promote build to TEST5 and TEST6</strong>: After QA confirmatio=
n, promote the build to TEST5 and TEST6 environments.</li>
<li><strong>Done</strong>: Workflow complete.</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>If tests fail, return to implementation and fix issues before proceeding=
.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>If code coverage or quality checks fail, address them and rerun tests.</=
p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>If PR is not approved, address review comments and update the PR.</p>
</blockquote>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
